+# Third native release acceptance review
+
+This contract separates stable-default acceptance from experimental source-selection quality. Native execution belongs to the coordinating root after its exact third-release build pin succeeds. All rows are pending until actual logs/output and private original source are reviewed; cached parity proves only the narrower tested contracts.
+
+## Stable legacy default
+
+Run native --selftest-notes-longform, --selftest-notes-truncation, --selftest-notes-context, --selftest-notes-evidence and parent-owned usage/app-hook checks. --selftest-notes-evidence runs both source-evidence and extractive-contract checks. Review the original stubborn/drop case's positive collapse/drop count and blank warning paragraph. Normal construction must retain original generated-facts prompts, plain transcript encoding, budgets/pass flow and typed cut disclosure. The SelfTest-false explicit option probe already passes in the corrected source harness; native normal startup/history remains its own gate.
+
+Use the guarded copied fixture with --selftest-meeting-notes-replay, explicit --notes-model and the same --notes-replay-window 8192 as the retained original mapped comparison. Omit --notes-source-indices for legacy; the result must label mode=legacy. Preserve exact model file/runtime/context pin and all original meeting bytes/preferences. Compare workflow/pass/token/collapse/drop/cut metadata and produced notes against the retained legacy result. Paragraph spacing is intentional. Legacy parity is not improved semantic quality: inherit and disclose its original attribution/coverage/future-intent failures.
+
+## Explicit source-ID experiment
+
+Run the same copied fixture/model/window with --notes-source-indices; the result must label mode=source-indices. This flag is distinct from --notes-selection-indices, which selects the failed whole extractive diagnostic. Preserve actual per-map/collapse raw arrays, admitted count, finish-by-limit and incomplete markers in private output. Confirm strict scope/original utterance identity and no unsupported map/collapse prose enters reduce. Empty/invalid output must stay visible as refusal/fallback; do not silently treat it as a successful comprehensive selection.
+
+Review both the source selections and final notes against the original full transcript and private reference notes. A correct selection can still be misrepresented by the final reduce. Use a private row per gold fact with source ID/time/speaker, admitted map/group, final-note representation, classification, unsupported additions and verdict. Do not copy these utterances or notes into this public document.
+
+| Gate | Required original-flow evidence | Reject condition |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Experience attribution | Both speakers' distinct experience and qualifications attached to the original speaker | Prototype and production/sourcing experience transferred between speakers, or speaker identity guessed |
+| Coverage | Main substantive distinctions and explanations throughout the full call preserved | Greetings/opening-only selection, generic topic labels, missing late material, or a larger count treated as proof |
+| Past and future | Completed activity distinguished from the future visit/question follow-up | Completed event turned into a task; future follow-up omitted or tense changed |
+| Deadline and owner | Every stated deadline/owner has explicit supporting source | Invented next-week deadline or responsible person; uncertain plan promoted to a firm dated commitment |
+| Decisions/actions/questions | Classification follows the actual utterance and its question/answer context | Greeting, explanation or hypothetical example classified as an action; resolved question presented as open |
+| Readability | Usable summary and enough concrete detail to review the meeting | Bare greetings, transcript fragments with missing antecedents, or unreadable excerpt dump |
+| Structural honesty | Actual cut/refusal/drop notice retained where applicable | incompleteFacts=false or generation OK cited as a semantic coverage verdict |
+| Cost | Same fixture/provider/window, measured input/output budget, wall/workflow time, passes and collapse/drop | Quality loss accepted solely for speed; extra context/passes hidden; instant/perfect claim without proof |
+
+There is no minimum-ID quota and no automatic checker/retry/model pass. More selected utterances may raise reduce/context cost. Record it honestly; retain failures. Full-input whole diagnostics must pass the actual preflight context count and remain experimental. The current Mini and Qwen whole-index failures are negative controls, not candidates for default promotion.
+
+## Privacy and completion
+
+Copied fixture/raw selections/rendered notes stay private; generic check output may stay public. Native replay private writer must not mirror payload to OS logs; verify absence using the test PID in root's existing diagnostic approach. Meeting/history/default preferences and original files must remain unchanged. No install/default strategy change until root's required acceptance is complete.
+
+If comprehensive mapped selection still misses gold facts or damages readability, retain the failed outputs and leave the semantic producer contract open. The stable legacy option permits independently verified capture/speaker/citation/performance work to install without introducing the new regression; that is not completion of the user's broader quality objective.
