+- The existing meeting health sample supplies bounded per-meeting peak and coverage
+  counters through its existing metadata save. Legacy records decode unknown coverage,
+  and older metadata writers cannot erase the same recording's accepted aggregate.
+  This is sampled observation, not continuous soak or a new production memory ceiling.
+- The existing local model pass records numeric prefill/decoded-input and generation
+  elapsed time. These include cooperative scheduling; they are neither nonstreaming
+  first-visible time nor the reference-machine ASR/voice decode floor.
+
+The diagnostic-only single-pass excerpt selector and typed temporal/intent comparison
+are experiments. They do not change the writer, model roles, settings, action execution
+or owner stores. Native semantic classification, factual coverage and readability are
+required before any promotion. Four intent neighborhoods are post-hoc copied windows,
+not exact unsaved original live snapshots; target-directed classification is narrower
+than complete production extraction.
+
+## Original evidence and pending native checks
+
+Actual-source original/fixed checks fail 6/23 then pass23 for map/collapse, and fail8/13
+then pass13 for action citation/confidence. Unrelated provider/store boundaries were
+substituted in those focused probes; native application acceptance is still pending.
+Speaker projection and performance observation have real isolated production-store
+consumer flags, also pending in the optimized bundle. Original owner context retained
+stale generic labels despite a final labelled transcript; only three rows are currently
+eligible for conservative exact binding in this private recording.
+
+See [acceptance plan](acceptance-plan.json), [notes evidence](../2026-10-07-notes-evidence/README.md),
+[action evidence](../2026-10-07-action-intent/README.md), and
+[speaker contract](../2026-10-07-quality-repair/speaker-projection/README.md).
+
+The build uses one shared source-quiet release compilation outside the synced repository,
+with two compiler jobs and a machine development-heavy relay claim. The default10GB
+free-space gate initially refused8.09GB; the explicit coordinated8GB gate passed with
+8.74GB free, swap6.51GB, load2.64 and no active owner meeting. The owner installed app is
+unchanged during verification. Compiler, native and model verdicts will be retained,
+including failures. No speedup, perfect notes, universal participant naming or new soak
+is declared by source-level checks.
+
+## First optimized native verdicts
+
+Candidate `b9dddc679fa89f999f40fa6accd95afc742f316c576f078c29b5111c1031d6b2`
+was built with invariant 1167 source/resource pins and stable signing. Evidence23,
+extractive contract18, reconciliation, longform, truncation, context assembly, health90,
+integrity67 and agent evidence89 passed. Performance failed2/17 at the actual saved
+clock boundary. Existing ISO8601 dates lose fractional seconds; the new summary now
+encodes its own reference-date doubles. Actual summary codec probe original fails3,
+corrected passes3; corrected native19 remains pending. Speaker projection failed1/39
+on its fixture's durable-vs-in-memory date comparison; test now compares separately
+against a saved baseline. The projection producer was unchanged by that test repair.
+
+The isolated store flag reported unchanged21files33defaults, while its embedded
+production tool-loop still failed18 inherited browser admission assertions. This
+failure remains open and is not converted into a pass by launcher exit0.
+
+The whole quote selection experiment failed with zero admitted records in71.63s.
+Raw selection was not retained by its early empty-result throw, so exact rejection
+reason is unproven. Prefill49.407s and generation13.220s are actual usage fields.
+Diagnostic visibility is repaired in source; indices-only selection is pending native.
+The eight targeted intent passes failed3 cases in29.50s wall. The genuine future
+follow-up was missed even in the first valid typed JSON object. JSON/schema/quote
+failures and semantic intent failure are separate. Targeted windows do not reproduce
+unsaved original inference snapshots. No classifier was promoted.
+
+Mapped evidence replay completed in203.57s versus the historical same model/window
+159.56s; this is not a controlled paired performance benchmark. All three maps hit
+600-token length; three additional collapses ran, only one fact reached reduce and
+two of three parts were dropped. The future follow-up remained absent. Native quality
+and cost are rejected: no promotion or installation of this writer. Source-ID
+selection through the same seams is the next bounded producer experiment. Private
+outputs stay outside Git; public usage and verdicts contain no meeting speech.
+
+### Diagnostic output privacy correction
+
+The first replay outputs were redirected to private files but `writeSelfTest` also
+mirrored each line into the local system log using public privacy. Earlier descriptions
+of private-only raw output were too broad. No cloud provider or relay received speech.
+Copied meeting notes/action/extractive harnesses now use the same failure-marker/output
+recorder with system-log mirroring disabled. Other self-test logging is unchanged.
+A SelfTest-only source-selection observer retains subsequent raw refusal evidence in
+the copied harness output, not production usage/store logs. Native process-scoped
+system-log absence remains pending; historical local logs are not erased.
+
+## Second native candidate, source freeze
+
+The first compile-coordination handoff mistakenly allowed source-only edits while the
+dictation debug build read the same whole app. All writers stopped; no verdict from
+changing-source builds is accepted. The peer's subsequent original/fixed native builds
+used invariant source snapshots and joined before this second release. Root applied
+cache-staged corrections only after that exact handoff. At claim, gate passed8.08GB
+free/swap7.04GB/load3.43. The second optimized build is pinned across1167 sources/resources.
+
+Map/collapse now selects a compact array of at most24 IDs present in its actual input.
+Code owns the complete original speech and source-derived clock/speaker. The same
+existing grouping seam carries typed source batches so collapse cannot borrow IDs
+from another group. Whitespace and integer terminals are bounded. No new production
+model pass, store or queue. Selection coverage and final fluent writing remain native
+quality gates. Copied replay retains raw selections through a defaultnil, SelfTest-only
+observer; its private writer bypasses the old public system-log mirror.
+
+The six-window action diagnostic uses actual extractor ingestion, production prompt/
+refine, one existing local provider call, application and persisted readback. Prior
+context is extractor-only reconstruction, not original unsaved state. Forwarding uses
+existing provider.complete to avoid importing foreign optional-runtime dependencies;
+quiet semantic/citation behavior is tested, not optional dispatch/pressure parity.
+Native malformed/cut output cannot count as a safe negative.
+
+An additional speaker producer gap was reproduced on unchanged14-check actual helper
+fixtures: original default labels erase confirmed attribution (RED4); the first
+correction wrongly rejects explicit user mappings for default labels (RED4). Corrected
+helper passes14, honoring explicit nonempty maps and refusing unmapped defaults. An
+initial probe compile used a non-main.swift top-level filename; unchanged test bytes
+were copied to main.swift, with the initial compiler failure retained. This source
+probe supplies no native service/store, ASR, acoustic identity or participant API proof;
+second-candidate actual committed-label consumer checks remain pending.
+
+## Second release results and rejected semantic candidate
+
+Second bundle `9b17a28e668cdbaac94fab2a85c2c31daa97c812172c577cc5dda8b1564154c7`
+compiled with invariant 1167 pins and stable signing. Actual saved performance19,
+speaker service/current/durable/manual-label51, evidence30 and extractive contract36
+pass, alongside longform, truncation, context, health90, integrity67 and agent evidence89.
+Owner isolation retained 21 files and 33 defaults unchanged; its inherited embedded
+browser production assertions remain FAILED. Nothing here promotes broader Agent readiness.
+
+The native MiniCPM source-ID map experiment completed in 54.97 s wall / 53.80 s
+producer duration, four passes and 106 generated tokens. All three maps selected only
+five of 519 speech utterances. Valid IDs and no structural truncation did not preserve
+substantive meeting coverage: real future follow-up, expertise attribution and important
+engineering/manufacturing distinctions were missing. This is a semantic FAIL and is
+not accepted for installation or production promotion. Under-selection occurs before
+reduce. A stronger selection contract is a hypothesis, not a proven fix.
+
+Sampled exact process footprint was 553,994,904 bytes and resident memory 2,131,771,392
+bytes over 26 two-second samples. These are sampled values, not continuous peaks or
+a reference-machine ASR/voice soak. Input/output/private selections remain outside Git.
+
+A retained native system-log query found 240 entries for the copied replay process and
+zero private diagnostic markers. The compiled private-writer branch bypasses the former
+public mirror; the observation is limited by retained logging and has no independent
+sentinel control. Historical local diagnostic mirrors were not erased. See
+`private-writer-native-log-query.json` and `second-native-tests.json`.
+
+### Native replay gate correction
+
+The default 10 GB free-disk gate declined at 6.94 GB. An orchestration check error
+launched the first immutable local model replay despite that failed command; the error
+was disclosed to the peer, and exclusive heavy ownership was then acquired separately.
+No compiler, download or source writes started. Subsequent bounded native replays use
+an explicit 5 GB free-disk / 8 GB swap gate: installed models are reused, no bundle is
+created, and output is small private diagnostics. The first measured explicit gate
+passed 6.94 GB free, 7.53 GB swap and load 2.71. Final build requires a fresh disk/claim
+audit and owned-artifact cleanup; this does not assert the original default gate passed.
+
+## Whole-source and actual action comparisons
+
+Whole-index Mini selects exactly the first 24 utterances, all Key points, in 96.83 s
+wall; substantive later discussion and future follow-up are absent. Whole-index Qwen3.5
+selects only the first two greeting sources in 151.00 s, and even classifies a greeting
+as Action items. Both semantic candidates FAIL; neither the larger model nor strict
+source copying establishes useful notes. No model/default promotion or owner mutation.
+
+Mini six-window production replay fails five windows in 23.81 s. Five raw replies omit
+the closing object brace well below the 400-token cap; one valid reply repeats schema
+placeholders as content. All action arrays are empty including a visible genuine future
+commitment. The live prompt itself also begins mid-labelled segment in all six original
+windows; reader and parser domains differ. A shared complete-segment producer seam and
+same-pass bounded output grammar are being staged separately from semantic acceptance.
+
+Qwen six-window run executes its first window but skips the remaining five before model
+entry. Retained native logs confirm a kernel warning-pressure event during the first
+call. Those unexecuted windows have no semantic verdict. The optional admission guard
+was retained; a single unchanged future-follow-up window is being tested in a fresh
+process without overriding pressure. Reconstructed extractor-only states and actual
+segment-end cutoffs remain explicit; these are not unsaved original model snapshots.
+
+## Legacy parity fixture correction in progress
+
+The first standalone legacy probes both compile but fail eight identical longform
+assertions; their stub does not exercise the intended collapse/drop boundary. The
+brief stub omits real labels (2813 vs 2934 characters), changing the measured budget
+from 734 to 704 fake tokens. Clock formatting also differs after one hour. These
+initial failures are retained; they are not passes or evidence of a production fix.
+An added no-context positive-drop assertion was also invalid for that exact provider
+budget. The revised same original stubborn/real-brief case must retain all original
+drop checks and assert the existing warning assembly has a paragraph separator.
+Exact real boundary formatting is being staged before re-running unchanged producer
+logic; no smaller transcript/window or weakened drop assertion.
+
+## Third source contract and release snapshot
+
+Third-loop admission: faster source-ID summaries are experimental and require explicit
+SelfTest opt-in; production keeps its original single/map/collapse/reduce prompt and
+budget contract. Corrected source parity and explicit production opt-in guard pass;
+initial shim failures remain retained. JSON shape, source evidence, semantic meaning,
+whole-meeting coverage and physical speed are distinct gates. Actual Mini action windows
+returned incomplete objects below400tokens; the producer now retains complete labelled
+utterances under the same3000-character boundary and sends one400-token constrained
+call. Source-owned primary evidence must still select the correct utterance; it does
+not prove future intent, recipient identity or an action permission. Original source
+contract fails11/27, corrected passes27, using substituted external boundaries; native
+sampler/semantic acceptance is pending. Source IDs cannot rescue a model that selects
+only greetings, and an empty result from malformed output is not a safe negative.
+
+Third release compilation failures are retained, with joined children before repairs:
+first the test writer actor annotation, then two pure JSON helpers required nonisolated
+annotations for scripted Sendable provider closures. These change test isolation only.
+The reused-cache build has an explicit6.5GB-free/8GB-swap coordination gate; the default
+10GB gate is not claimed to pass. Compilerjobs2 does not cap Swift's internal WMO threads.
+New physical ASR/voice soak, actual provider participant/name bindings, legacy full-note
+semantic omissions and the inherited browser production gate remain open.
+
+See corrected [legacy parity](../2026-10-07-notes-evidence/legacy-parity/README.md), [native notes acceptance](../2026-10-07-notes-evidence/native-acceptance.md) and [action input contract](../2026-10-07-action-intent/source-contract/README.md).
