+# Fresh single future window: Qwen3.5
+
+FAIL original citation flow. One actual production call returns valid JSON and recognizes
+the genuine future follow-up, without inventing a deadline in this completion. It cites
+a partial antecedent/past-event segment and composes evidence across a second source
+fragment separated by microphone acknowledgments. That string is not contiguous in
+the cited segment, so the producer correctly rejects it and saves no candidate.
+
+The actual action-bearing source fragment is visible. A proposed producer contract
+lets the model select that primary segment while code owns exact original evidence;
+this is a hypothesis until the fixed native chooses the right anchor. Old supplied
+quote validation must remain strict; malformed legacy rows may not gain a new fallback.
+Recipient names occur in an earlier fragment; the evidence-local recipient contract
+remains unchanged. No execution authority or new identity claim is supplied.
+
+Wall 17.02 s. Same original speech/window, extractor-only seed, one fresh process,
+pressure admission retained. This refines the diagnosis: meaning was recognized here,
+but citation copying failed. It does not retroactively turn earlier malformed/Mini
+outputs or skipped Qwen windows into semantic passes.
